+\subsection{Reproducibility and bounded stopping}
+The controlled implementation checks Stop before each proposal trial and
+finishes any in-progress atomic proposal before saving. Checkpoints retain
+geometry, counts, exact ownership and member ordering, shuffled vertex
+order, generator state, cached normal variate, last completed round, and
+the next root/trial position. Resume skips a shuffle already performed
+for a partial round. Full-round termination semantics are retained.
